  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The M with a wall pass – pass, return and shoot",
  "description": "A development of the M. Two lines in the corners at one end and a cone on each side further out. A runs up along the board, goes around their cone and gets a pass from B in the opposite corner. A plays it back to B, gets the ball again and shoots – preferably first time. Then B starts from the other side.\n\nMake sure the players really run out and around the cone. Otherwise they end up too close to goal, the drill loses pace and it gets crowded. The shot can well be a backhand, since the goal is close. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Run all the way around the cone – shortcuts kill the tempo."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The return pass should be first time and firm."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Try a backhand shot – the distance is short."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "focus": [
    "passing",
    "shooting"
  ],
  "phase": "warmup",
